.TH REPOCTL 1 "September 2026" "Repora 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
repoctl \- deterministic, policy-driven Git repository management CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B repoctl
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B repoctl
.BR --help
.br
.B repoctl
.BR --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B repoctl
manages configured canonical Git repositories and mirrors, and collects read-only repository posture evidence.
Mirror configuration is read from a SCHEMA-0001 YAML file, named
.B repora.yaml
by default.
.PP
Repora is fail-closed around destructive mirror updates. Configuration declares repository identity and topology; credentials and mutation authority are supplied separately at runtime.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Inspect canonical and mirror default-branch state.
.TP
.B plan
Show planned mirror updates or emit an exact executable plan artifact.
.TP
.B apply
Apply current observations or an exact plan artifact.
.TP
.B sync
Alias for
.BR apply .
.TP
.B posture
Collect, converge, and evaluate repository posture evidence. Collector subcommands include
.BR inventory ,
.BR docs ,
.BR hooks ,
.BR commits ,
and
.BR mirrors .
.TP
.B plan-readme
Review managed README changes or emit an exact managed-artifact plan.
.TP
.B apply-readme
Dry-run or apply an exact managed README plan with journaled evidence.
.TP
.B validate-report
Validate a repository assessment report without mutation.
.TP
.B list-findings
List findings from a validated assessment report.
.TP
.B generate-scorecard
Render scorecard dimensions from a validated assessment report without recalculation.
.TP
.B assess
Create a canonical assessment skeleton without overwriting an existing file.
.TP
.B version
Show embedded version and commit metadata.
.TP
.B help
Show command help.
.SH MIRROR OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -f " file"
Path to SCHEMA-0001 YAML configuration. Default:
.BR repora.yaml .
.TP
.B --json
Print stabilized command JSON where supported.
.TP
.B --artifact
With
.B plan
or
.BR plan-readme ,
print the exact review/execution artifact as JSON.
.TP
.BI --plan-file " file"
Execute the exact reviewed plan artifact from
.IR file .
.TP
.BI --parallel " n"
Maximum concurrent repository operations. Default: 5.
.TP
.B --continue-on-error
Continue processing other repositories after an error.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Show what a supported apply operation would change without mutation.
.TP
.B --force
Allow destructive mirror overwrites for ahead or diverged mirrors. This option does not apply to managed README mutation.
.TP
.B --debug
Print debug logs to standard error.
.SH POSTURE
The
.B posture inventory
action observes repository and CI facts through a GET-only provider boundary.
.B posture docs,
.B posture hooks,
and
.B posture commits
collect bounded read-only evidence for their respective domains.
.B posture mirrors
reuses Repora's local reconciliation observation path and may refresh local cache state, but does not push or synchronize mirrors.
.PP
.B posture converge
and
.B posture report
are offline-only. They consume versioned artifacts, preserve unknown or unavailable evidence, and do not contact providers or mutate repository state.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GITHUB_TOKEN
Optional GitHub token used by provider-protected read operations.
.TP
.B GH_TOKEN
Alternative optional GitHub token.
.TP
.B REPORA_CACHE_DIR
Absolute path overriding the default local mirror cache root.
.PP
Git transport credentials may also be supplied through the operator's normal Git or SSH credential mechanisms. Credentials must not be embedded in
.B repora.yaml
or packaged example configuration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B repora.yaml
Default SCHEMA-0001 repository topology configuration in the current working directory.
.TP
.B ~/.cache/repora
Default local cache root when
.B REPORA_CACHE_DIR
is unset.
.TP
.B share/repora/examples/repora.yaml
Non-secret example configuration installed with packaged distributions.
.TP
.B share/repora/schemas/
Versioned public JSON schemas installed with packaged distributions.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect configured repository state:
.PP
.nf
repoctl status -f repora.yaml
.fi
.PP
Review a deterministic mirror plan:
.PP
.nf
repoctl plan -f repora.yaml --artifact > plan.json
.fi
.PP
Preflight an exact plan without mutation:
.PP
.nf
repoctl apply -f repora.yaml --plan-file plan.json --dry-run --json
.fi
.PP
Collect GitHub repository posture without mutation:
.PP
.nf
repoctl posture inventory OWNER/REPO
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Installing Repora grants no repository or provider authority by itself. Keep credentials, host-specific topology, and other sensitive operator state outside Nix derivations and release artifacts. Review exact plans before mutation and preserve Repora's stale-state and lease checks rather than replaying old evidence.
.PP
Source visibility, binary stripping, or resistance to disassembly is not a security boundary. Security-sensitive authority must remain in explicit credentials, policy, validation, and runtime controls.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation and release notes are published with the Repora source repository at
.UR https://github.com/hackelia-micrantha/repora
.UE
